Z||000006||007DOUG||01-04-2001||07:49 PM||||Damn Tim, Thats one sweet GT.<P>I swear I could smell those leather seats.<P>Hey, thats what a GT steering wheel looked like when new? NICE.<P>You really have to admire someone that can buy a car, and never drive it. That would be really difficult for me......especially a T-top GT. I wouldn't drive it everyday, just cruise around in the summer.<P>So, what the story behind the car? Was it a dealer's car that sat on the showroom all its life? I've heard of an 88 T-top GT on a dealer's showroom in CA. Is this it?<P>I'm surprised how many 88 GTs (and occassionaly Indys) are tucked away.....still on MSO. There's an 88 GT (red, sunroof, auto) in Hemmings this month with 19 miles for example.<P>Just one more Q: Does yours have a sub?<P>Tim, You're my new best friend.||||reg||14
