Z||000015||fieroparts.com||01-05-2001||11:44 AM||||Does every last Fiero have to be driven? I have a Fiero I drive, 1988 coupe 3.4 with Firebird GTA seats with twin power lumbar, head up display (and it works) poly and kyb’s on all four ends, all options added, Borla<BR>Exhaust, 120mph GT gauges, pw,pl,pm the works.   I do get to drive a Fiero.  I get just as much pleasure  from my 88GT as I do my 88 Coupe on the road. I think it is important to keep some of these cars 100% original.<P>If you want to pay the big bucks for a NEW Fiero and drive it till it is almost worthless that’s your choice.<BR>to each his own.  Thanks<P><BR>Take a look at these pictures: <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe1.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe2.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe3.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/hud2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/hud2.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/hud3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/hud3.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/lumbar1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/lumbar1.jpg</A> <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>What the heck good is a car that you can't or don't dare drive? It then becomes a usless shrine. Drive and enjoy the sucker.  Don't get mad anyone.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>1988 GT  000117.1 MILES T-TOPS LOADED MED. RED<BR>AS NEW AS THEY GET!||||reg||7
